<title>USA: U.S. High Court rules against ex-asbestos makers.</title>
<headline>U.S. High Court rules against ex-asbestos makers.</headline>
<dateline>WASHINGTON 1997-06-25</dateline>
<text>
<p>The U.S. Supreme Court Wednesday handed a defeat to 20 former asbestos manufacturers by refusing to reinstate a proposed $1.3 billion settlement involving an estimated 100,000 personal injury claims.</p>
<p>The justices upheld a U.S. appeals court ruling that threw out the settlement on the grounds that it raises questions of fairness in how it treats the future claims of people who had been exposed to asbestos but are not yet sick.</p>
</text>
